# Reading a report

```
Error: Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch: This value is String (text), but `f` returns Int
 More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch
Run `jet explain Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch` to learn more
```

A lint heading such as `Lint: Jet.UnusedImport: …` names its lint, and
`#Allow(Jet.UnusedImport, "kept for the demo")` keeps it quiet Jet.UnusedImport.
A library's own `Error: game.FrameHold: …` keeps its name.
A runtime stop reads `Stop: Jet.Panic: …` and links jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.Panic.
The report object `{"code":"E0113","name":"Jet.ReturnTypeMismatch","what":"x"}` gains its name.
`jet.NotARegisteredDiagnostic` names no row and stays.
